# Patch: Dion with compressed synchronization across optimizer instances (optional set "dion",
# applied after the muon-zero1 set; launch.sh OPTIMIZER=dion-zero1)
#
# Problem:   with GLOBAL_DP>1 (ddp.num_distributed_optimizer_instances) the gradient shards of every
#            matrix are all-reduced between the instances once per step (~4.6 GB per GPU per step at
#            8 nodes, the simulated inter-datacenter link). Megatron-Core has no Dion.
# What:      megatron/core/optimizer/dion.py: Dion (Ahn et al. 2025, arXiv:2504.05295; written from
#            the paper) for the shard-aligned layer-wise optimizer: per matrix B = M + G,
#            P = orth(B Q), R = B^T P, M = B - (1 - mu) P R^T, Q = colnorm(R), X -= lr scale P Q^T;
#            equal-shape matrices batched (stacked momentum and Q, Cholesky QR2 in fp64 with a
#            Householder fallback). Registered as emerging optimizer 'dion' (optimizer=dist_dion),
#            non-matrix params on Adam as for Muon, update scale as muon_scale_mode (full rank =
#            Muon's update size). ddp.layer_wise_skip_inter_instance_grad_sync: DDP does not
#            all-reduce the matrix gradient shards across instances (with averaging collectives it
#            divides them by N instead, so that they add up to the global mean); Dion keeps one
#            momentum per instance and sums only B Q and B^T P over the inter-instance group,
#            (m + n) r instead of m n values per matrix, exactly equivalent to Dion on the global
#            gradient (see dion.py). Grad norm for clipping: sqrt(N sum_i |g_i|^2) over the
#            instances (identical on all of them). Momenta averaged across instances before a
#            checkpoint is saved (exact no-op); Q not checkpointed (same seed after a resume).
#            OptimizerConfig dion_* fields; TP = expert TP = 1 only.
# Porting:   _get_megatron_emerging_optimizer and LayerWiseDistributedOptimizer as changed by
#            muon-zero1/0002; the inter-instance all-reduce loop in
#            _ParamAndGradBucketGroup.start_grad_sync.
#
